#!/usr/bin/env python
"""Write every Cloudflare CNAME record pointing at a Pantheon platform domain to JSON.

TEMPORARY.  Delete after Pantheon's Fastly -> Pantheon-Cloudflare CDN migration completes; see
development/2026-07-30-platform-domain-util2/SPEC.md section 11 for the checklist.

Standalone by design: this imports nothing from psh/, check/, plugin/ or script_context, so most
of removing it is `git rm` of the script, its .py symlink and its test file.  The credential
read, the account/zone/record walk and the atomic write are COPIES of plugin/cloudflare/fqdns.py
and plugin/cloudflare/client.py; normalize()/is_platform_domain() are copies of
find-platform-domains-dns.

Unlike fqdns.json, this considers ALL records in ALL zones -- not just proxied ones -- and keeps
only CNAMEs whose target ends in .pantheonsite.io.  Naming zones on the command line narrows the
sweep to those zones (SPEC A1.3); with none, every zone in every visible account is swept.  The
output is produced in full on every run, whatever the age of anything already on disk.

Output: FOUR files in basename mode (-o/--output-basename BASENAME -- a `.` anywhere in the FINAL
path component of BASENAME is fatal; directory components may contain dots): BASENAME.json (the
inventory -- every platform CNAME, keyed by normalized FQDN, with its zone_name and the A/AAAA
addresses its target resolves to), BASENAME-plan.json (the forward rewrite: platform CNAME ->
resolved A/AAAA, one Cloudflare batch call per FQDN), BASENAME-revert.json (that batch call's
reverse) and BASENAME-excluded.json (every FQDN that got no plan entry, with one of eight reason
codes -- see classify()'s docstring -- and why).  Without -o, only the inventory goes to stdout and
no other file is written.  EVERY run resolves each entry's target for A and AAAA and applies the
same eight exclusion gates in BOTH modes, so the inventory is identical either way -- only its
destination differs.  Ambiguous FQDNs (more than one platform CNAME for the same name) are omitted
from the inventory entirely, in both modes.  The conventional organization-wide-baseline invocation
is now:

    find-platform-domains-cloudflare -o platform-domains-cloudflare

-o rather than `> platform-domains-cloudflare.json`: the shell truncates a redirect target BEFORE
the sweep starts, so any failed run leaves a zero-byte file where the baseline was, while -o writes
a temp file and os.replace()s each of the four files only on success (per file -- the four are not
atomic as a SET; see write_outputs()'s docstring for the accepted residual).

Every operator message -- warnings, progress, the summary, errors -- goes to stderr.  Exit 0 =
output produced with nothing excluded, 1 = produced but at least one FQDN was excluded (NEW in
this increment -- see the eight reason codes in classify()'s docstring), 2 = could not complete,
130 = interrupted; a doomed stdout or stderr is a named exit 2, NOT the interpreter's 120, which is
what require_usable_streams/report_line/write_json_stdout exist for.  The stated exception,
exhaustive: argparse writes its usage, error and --help text before those guards exist and outside
every handler, so BOTH `--help >/dev/full` and `--bogus 2>/dev/full` still exit 120.

Requires: the `cloudflare` SDK (declared under this project's `cloudflare` extra, which the
documented `uv pip install .[mysql,aws,cloudflare]` setup line installs) and Cloudflare
credentials in the [Cloudflare] section of the config file.
"""
